parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T13:11:30.015Z",codex-agent,"PR #92 second-review check reconfirms the existing discontinuities: full health --strict-exit reports history_drift_chain_mismatch for pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih. A fresh no-local clone of prior head c511d607579d746e201a15e54a37b287c79b1195 reproduces both; those items and history streams remain unchanged by this review. The documented CI command health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit passes and must not be reported as verification of these older chains. Preserve this existing follow-up open; no re-anchor, repair or rewrite performed."
  "2026-10-21T11:12:40.192Z",codex-agent,"PR 101 review-round supplementary full health with pinned pm-cli 2026.10.21 confirms the same two existing chain mismatches in pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih. Both item/history files are unchanged relative to origin/main and the review candidate. Full health checks 74 items and reports two chain mismatches, zero hash mismatches, zero workspace-state mismatches. No existing records were rewritten. This is independent of the release-check and default CI health gates, which do not establish full history integrity."
  "2026-10-23T19:09:49.301Z",codex-agent,PR 110 review round confirms the two already tracked chain mismatches for pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih. Both item/history pairs are unchanged from origin/main. Full local health authority remains ok but reports these historical advisories plus local extension and merge-driver configuration warnings. No append-only history was repaired or rewritten. Release and CI check-only health evidence is separate from verification of these older chains.
  "2026-11-12T05:47:22.899Z",codex-agent,"PR #165 round-five supplementary full health with pinned pm-cli 2026.11.11 confirms the same two previously tracked history_drift_chain_mismatch findings for pm-rust-bj7a and pm-rust-unih. Both item/history pairs are byte-identical to HEAD and origin/main. node tests/oracle/launch.mts health --strict-exit --json exits one; the unchanged CI gate node tests/oracle/launch.mts health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit exits zero. The check-only pass does not certify these historical chains. No records were repaired, rewritten or re-anchored. Existing follow-up remains open and unclaimed; evidence is also in docs/ORACLE_REVIEW_ROUND5_2026_11_12.md."
  "2026-11-17T02:59:23.959Z",codex-sol,"PR #168 repairs the two historical chain discontinuities from #109 using pm history-repair. The release history-prefix gate currently rejects that audited re-anchor as history_prefix_replaced. Plan: preserve raw-prefix enforcement for ordinary changes, validate exact repair marker and original-record evidence for hash-only re-anchors, delegate chain replay to the published pm verifier, and add positive and tampering regression tests. The two open review threads were read; no review-thread changes are planned."
  "2026-11-17T03:05:24.424Z",codex-sol,"The gate now accepts only a final history_repair marker using the published default re-anchor message, identical pre-marker record count and order, hash-only field changes, and one appended reanchor_evidence entry containing the exact original record per rewritten event. The marker count must match. The pinned published CLI verifies full record/evidence integrity and chain replay against the paired item. Existing guidance and provenance advisories remain tracked by pm-rust-vuwe; no unrelated history normalization is included."
  "2026-11-17T03:09:35.343Z",codex-sol,"Final targeted validation: pm test pm-rust-b4yl --run --progress ran node --test scripts/crash-history-prefix.test.mts: 26 passed, zero failures or skips. node scripts/crash-history-prefix.mts --base origin/main passes with three changed histories, including the two repairs. cargo fmt --check, npm run changelog:check, harness tsc, targeted ESLint and git diff --check pass. No Rust code changed, so clippy is not required. Full pm health --strict-exit has no history drift; it exits one for inherited merge-driver configuration drift in the package worktree. A fresh clone exits one only for gate-failing merge_driver_configuration_missing, alongside the two pre-existing advisory classes owned by pm-rust-vuwe. The requested no-other-findings condition is not met. Evidence and exception details are in docs/HISTORY_REPAIR_PREFIX_GATE_2026_11_17.md. Full release certification is left to CI."
  "2026-11-17T03:10:48.634Z",codex-sol,"Publication blocker: the branch already contains an inherited merge commit with a Git author outside the required commit identity. The required origin/main..HEAD author check therefore fails despite all new commits using the required identity. The implementation and validation evidence are committed locally. A branch rebuild with a guarded force-push, or an explicit inherited-author exception, requires owner direction before publication. The PR body update is prepared, preserving existing sections and adding Gate change. No push or review-thread action has occurred."
